#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:8
msgid "microstack-support interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `microstack-support` interface enables multiple service access for the "
"_Microstack infrastructure_. It's used by the [Microstack](https://"
"microstack.run/) snap, a full OpenStack deployment within a single snap "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Virtual machines are spawned as QEMU processes with libvirt acting as a "
"management daemon (including for activities such as applying AppArmor "
"profiles)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"Networking is provided largely via OpenVSwitch and Neutron, with dnsmasq "
"acting as an auxiliary daemon. A tun/tap kernel module is used for creating "
"virtual interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"Virtual machines rely on KVM for virtualisation acceleration and the vhost "
"framework in the kernel (vhost_net, vhost_scsi, vhost_vsock)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:19
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:21
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"The `microstack-support` plug is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-unsupported>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/microstack-support-interface.md:28
